<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Batticaloa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Batticaloa is a city on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, built around a large lagoon in the Eastern Province. The Portuguese built a fort there in the 1620s, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> captured in 1638 with the help of the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a>, opening their conquest of the island's coasts. The city has a mainly Tamil-speaking population and was badly hit by the 2004 tsunami.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/batticaloa.jpg" alt="Batticaloa" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Croos · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sea_Fishing,_Batticaloa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
